Wikipedia: Signs of AI writing
------------------------------
The pattern categories in references/ai-tells.md also draw on "Wikipedia:Signs
of AI writing", https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Signs_of_AI_writing,
maintained by WikiProject AI Cleanup and other contributors under the Creative
Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 License
(https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/). The descriptions and
examples in this repository are written in our own words and no text from that
page is reproduced. The short watch lists of commonly flagged single words and
stock phrases in references/ai-tells.md and scripts/check_ai_tells.py (such as
"delve" or "it is important to note") name the same well-known tells.

US federal plain-language examples
----------------------------------
corpus/attested/plain-language-pairs.json contains before/after rewrites
published by US federal agencies under the Plain Writing Act, as archived at
https://github.com/GSA/plainlanguage.gov. As works of the US Government they
are in the public domain (17 U.S.C. 105).
